ars to have resided at Magdala, east of Jordan, a distance of nearly ninety miles. Add to this, that our Saviour seems to have been now in or near Nain, not at Bethany; and the woman appears from the recital to have been previously unknown to him.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-7-46","title":"Luke 7:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>Ru 3:3; 2Sa 14:2; Ps 23:5; 104:15; Ec 9:8; Da 10:3; Am 6:6; Mic 6:15 Mt 6:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-7-47","title":"Luke 7:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>Her. 42; 5:20,21; Ex 34:6,7 which. Isa 1:18; 55:7; Eze 16:63; 36:29-32; Mic 7:19; Ac 5:31; Ro 5:20 1Co 6:9-11; 1Ti 1:14; 1Jo 1:7 she. 43; Mt 10:37; Joh 21:15-17; 2Co 5:14; Ga 5:6; Eph 6:24; Php 1:9 1Jo 3:18; 4:19; 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-7-48","title":"Luke 7:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>Thy. Mt 9:2; Mr 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-7-49","title":"Luke 7:49","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":49,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":49},"content":"<p>Who. 5:20,21; Mt 9:3; Mr 2:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-7-50","title":"Luke 7:50","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":50,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":50},"content":"<p>Thy. 8:18,42,48; 18:42; Hab 2:4; Mt 9:22; Mr 5:34; 10:52; Eph 2:8-10 Jas 2:14-26 go. Ec 9:7; Ro 5:1,2</p>"}]}